[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Views nest by Contains and PLACE, never by composite nodes, section elements or included documents

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[DECISION]
UID: DEC-FILES-STAY-FLAT-FOR-VIEWS
TITLE: Views nest by Contains and PLACE, never by composite nodes, section elements or included documents
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATUS: accepted
RETIRES_ON: The scribe learns to walk nested nodes and a view needs nesting one file cannot express with Contains.
STATEMENT: >>>
strictdoc can nest: a composite element holds nodes inside one file, a
SECTION element declared in the grammar nests with numbering, and
DOCUMENT_FROM_FILE assembles one-node files into a tree. All three were
measured on 2026-08-30 (EV-COMPOSITE-NARRATIVE-COSTS) and refused for
views: a composite element refuses the plain form, so every narrative would
be rewritten; the scribe's walk is flat, so it lists, checks and shows only
the top node of a nested file; included documents export as unnamed
sections and drop out of the document list. Views nest with Contains and
say how with PLACE. One node per file stands.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Nesting inside a file buys nothing the flat form with PLACE cannot say, and costs the scribe, the checks and one-node-per-file.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Ruled 2026-08-30 as a first-pass decision under the operator's delegation ('I don't want to be bothered by the recommendation before implementation'); overrule by superseding. Chosen from three independent designs judged against an 82-element inventory of the v1 page. AUTHORED_BY reads llm because the writer has no flag for the human rungs.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: EV-COMPOSITE-NARRATIVE-COSTS
  ROLE: Proven_By
